  "body": "Consider\r\n```html\r\n<div contenteditable>\r\n  <span>hello world</span>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\nBrowsers all treat the `div` element as a focusable area for the purpose of `element.focus()`. However, they do not treat the `span` element as focusable: when one calls `span.focus()`, `document.activeElement` gets set to the document `body`. It might be worth it to add an additional item to the [focusable area](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#focusable-area) definition.\r\n\r\nFor anyone interested, Blink implements this [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/master:third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/element.cc;l=4368;drc=c1b3b0cbacc3033bd0aee8725065be9a0e8d6701). Blink also supports the non-standard `-webkit-user-modify` CSS property that provides much of the same access to the code underlying `contenteditable` (and I assume WebKit does also), though Firefox does not.",
